      "text": "Subsection 39(1) states that the Registrar must reject an application if the trade mark contains or consists of a sign that, under regulations made for the purposes of section 18, is not to be used as a trade mark. There are currently no regulations made for the purposes of section 18, which means grounds for rejection under s 39(1) are not raised during examination."
